        <version_id>1.0</version_id>
        <title>Shape model of (486958) Arrokoth: arrokoth_porter_2024_v01</title>
        <information_model_version>1.19.0.0</information_model_version>
        <product_class>Product_Ancillary</product_class>
        <Citation_Information>
            <author_list>Porter, S.</author_list>
            <editor_list>Singer, K.; Enke, B.; Gobat, C.; Crombie, M. K.; Keeney, B.; Parker, J. Wm.</editor_list>
            <publication_year>2024</publication_year>
            <description>This is an updated shape model of Kuiper Belt Object (KBO) 2014 MU69
                (486958 Arrokoth) with 40960 triangular faces and 20484 vertices. It uses all
                resolved images of Arrokoth obtained by the New Horizons LOng Range Reconnaissance
                Imager (LORRI) before, during, and after the Arrokoth fly-by on January 1, 2019.

                See pre-print paper Porter, et al. (2024b) for detailed information about the
                construction process and tool versions used. All distance units are kilometers.
                The orbital period of Arrokoth is 0.6632553 days. Its pole orientation is
                RA = 317.4880752°, DEC = -24.8876496° in the International Celestial Reference
                Frame (ICRF). The prime meridian is 184.4589465° (at epoch = BODY2486958_PM).
            </description>
        </Citation_Information>
        <Modification_History>
            <Modification_Detail>
                <modification_date>2024-10-02</modification_date>
                <version_id>1.0</version_id>
                <description>Initial release of the 2024 Arrokoth shape model as part of the K7 delivery.</description>
            </Modification_Detail>
        </Modification_History>
    </Identification_Area>
